  "finding": {
    "risk": "zte_touch_pdev_unregister clears cdev+0xdd0 before platform_device_unregister. A manual bind in that interval could otherwise make the name-matched synthetic child pass the slot-identity check and enter the main touchscreen probe.",
    "change": "zte_touch_probe_dispatch now rejects a missing OF node or a node that is not compatible with zte_tp before consulting tpd_cdev. The synthetic child is created by platform_device_alloc(\"zte_touch\", PLATFORM_DEVID_NONE), receives no OF node, and the registration helper does not assign one. The real target node uses compatible = \"zte_tp\".",
    "result": "The current candidate disassembly contains the OF-node null check, the direct of_device_is_compatible call and the existing child-slot check. The synthetic child therefore remains rejected even after the slot is cleared. The dispatch callback KCFI type ID is 0xc7f8c87c, matching the stock zte_touch_probe callback type.",
    "status_effect": "The zte_touch_pdev_unregister mapping remains HARDENED_STOCK_DEVIATION / INTENTIONAL_HARDENING_DEVIATION. The global map remains PARTIAL_SOURCE_MAP; this focused review does not revalidate or promote all 367 mappings."
  },
